From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sunshineinabox <aqemail@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 14:00:00 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] interconnect: qcom: icc-rpm: program all three bits of the
 BIMC priority fields

The PRIOLVL and AREQPRIO fields of the BIMC BKE health registers are
three bits wide on the SM6115: Qualcomm's bengal BIMC definitions give
the registers a mask of 0x80000707, and on a MANGMI Air X a write of
0x80000707 to the TCU port's HEALTH0 reads back unchanged.

icc-rpm masks the fields with 0x3 and 0x300, so a priority of 4 to 7
loses its top bit. The TCU ports of SM6115, QCM2290 and Shikra ask for
priority 6 and got 2, below what the vendor driver gives the SMMU's
table walks.

Widen the masks to 0x7 and 0x700. The other icc-rpm tables use
priorities of 3 or less, so their writes do not change.

Tested on a MANGMI Air X with 0139: all four TCU health registers read
0x606 after boot and after three suspends to vmin.

Signed-off-by: sunshineinabox <aqemail@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/interconnect/qcom/icc-rpm.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/interconnect/qcom/icc-rpm.c b/drivers/interconnect/qcom/icc-rpm.c
index b3da614..3de2e68 100644
--- a/drivers/interconnect/qcom/icc-rpm.c
+++ b/drivers/interconnect/qcom/icc-rpm.c
@@ -29,8 +29,8 @@
 #define M_BKE_HEALTH_CFG_ADDR(i, n)	(M_BKE_REG_BASE(n) + 0x40 + (0x4 * i))
 
 #define M_BKE_HEALTH_CFG_LIMITCMDS_MASK	0x80000000
-#define M_BKE_HEALTH_CFG_AREQPRIO_MASK	0x300
-#define M_BKE_HEALTH_CFG_PRIOLVL_MASK	0x3
+#define M_BKE_HEALTH_CFG_AREQPRIO_MASK	0x700
+#define M_BKE_HEALTH_CFG_PRIOLVL_MASK	0x7
 #define M_BKE_HEALTH_CFG_AREQPRIO_SHIFT	0x8
 #define M_BKE_HEALTH_CFG_LIMITCMDS_SHIFT 0x1f
 
